; ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
; RESOLUTION-AFFECTING SETTINGS ARE GUARDED. infra/ci/npmrc-guard.mjs
; ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
; Every line in this file applies to EVERY npm resolution with no command line
; to inspect: Dockerfile:31, the pre-merge gate, lockfile-maintenance.yml's
; deliberately-bare refresh steps, Dependabot's updater, and your laptop. A
; setting added here silently overrides flags chosen per-site for measured
; reasons. The guard fails on any resolution-affecting key that is not on the
; record; adding one with a reason and a measurement makes it green.
;
; 🚨 `legacy-peer-deps=true` IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT. droplinked-shopfront#693
; adopted it; adopting it here is the wrong move and was measured to be.
; On dev @ 21956bf, npm 10.9.3, node 22.18.0:
;
;   committed lockfile, `npm ci`                     890 packages, 3 unmet edges
;   committed lockfile, `npm ci --legacy-peer-deps`  890 packages, 3 unmet edges
;   regenerate in place, no flag                     0-line lockfile diff
;   clean regen WITH legacy-peer-deps=true           839 packages, 8 unmet edges
;
; Rows 1-3 are the point: the committed lockfile and the resolver already
; AGREE, and the flag changes nothing about what `npm ci` installs, because
; `npm ci` installs the lockfile rather than resolving. Row 4 is what the
; setting would actually do — drop 70 lockfile entries, among them
; @droplinked_inc/wallet-connection and @droplinked_inc/web3-kit, the declared
; peers of the first-party runtime package @droplinked_inc/web3 — while
; `next build` and `npm test` both stay GREEN. A change to what ships that no
; gate in this repository can see.
;
; The condition #693 fixed does not exist here. There, Dependabot's
; `npm install --force --package-lock-only` diverged from the workflow's
; install and re-minted `"peer": true` nodes on every rebase. Here,
; regeneration in place is byte-identical to what is committed.
;
; See also lockfile-maintenance.yml, which already records the same finding
; from the other direction and keeps its refresh steps bare on purpose.

registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
save-exact=false
audit-level=high
